Privacy Policy
Corporate Dominance
Twelve52 LLC

Last updated: October 4, 2026

Corporate Dominance ("the App") is developed by Twelve52 LLC ("we", "us", "our"). This policy explains what information is collected when you use the App, by whom, and why.

No account, no personal details. The App does not ask for your name, email address or any other personal details, and it works without an account. We do not sell information about you.

Game data. Your saves, settings and progress are stored on your device. If you are signed in to Google Play Games, your active save is also stored in your own Google Play Games account so you can continue on another device. We do not have access to it.

Feedback and bug reports. If you choose to send feedback or report a bug from Settings, the text you type is sent to our server together with the App build number, your platform and operating system version, your device model, the App language, and a fingerprint of your current save (a seed and a quarter number, so we can reproduce a bug). Nothing identifies you personally unless you write it in the message. Reports are read by us and kept only as long as needed to act on them.

Remote settings. At launch the App reads balance settings, in-app announcements, language packs and the list of our other games from our server (hosted by Supabase). These are read-only downloads; the request carries no account or advertising identifier.

Advertising (Google AdMob). The App shows banner, interstitial and rewarded ads through Google AdMob. Google may collect device identifiers (including the advertising ID), IP address and usage data to serve and measure ads, personalized or not depending on your choices. Where the law requires it (in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, for example) the App first shows Google's consent form, before the ad SDK starts. Where the consent form applies, an Ad privacy options button appears in the App's Settings, and you can reset or delete your advertising ID in your device settings at any time. Google's privacy policy: policies.google.com/privacy.

Analytics (Firebase). The App uses Google Firebase Analytics for two things only: attribution of app installs to our advertising, and ad revenue reporting. It records app installs and sessions, purchases, ad impressions and one gameplay event (a fiscal quarter resolved), tied to an app instance identifier that Firebase generates. We do not log what you do inside the game beyond that, and we build no profiles. No names, no email addresses. Collection starts only after the consent step above. Firebase's privacy information: firebase.google.com/support/privacy.

Google Play Games. If you sign in, Google handles your profile, achievements and leaderboard entries under its own privacy policy.

In-app purchases. Purchases are processed entirely by Google Play. We never see or store payment information.

Notifications. Reminders are optional and stay off until you turn them on in the App's Settings. They are scheduled on your device; no notification token is sent to us. You can turn them off in the App's Settings or in your device settings at any time.

A game, not advice. The App is a simulation. The companies and people in it are invented. Nothing in it is financial, legal, tax or investment advice.

Children. The App is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. The advertising described above applies to all players.

Retention. Reports are deleted once resolved or after 12 months at most. Everything else lives on your device or in your own Google Play Games account and is removed when you delete the App or the account data. Abandon this run in the App's Settings deletes the current save from your device and from Google Play Games.

Your choices. Reset or delete your advertising ID in your device settings (Settings > Privacy > Ads), open the ad privacy options in the App's Settings where they are offered, buy Remove Ads to stop banner and interstitial ads, leave reminders off, or play without signing in to Google Play Games to keep your save on the device only.

Changes. Updates to this policy appear on this page with a new date.

